WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:07.920
It happened an age ago.
&nbsp;

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:14.000
She's talking about the shattering of the Elden&nbsp;
Ring. An entire age has passed, since then.
&nbsp;

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:19.280
But when I recall, I see it true.
This character with four arms,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:24.160
and pale, brittle skin, was a witness.
On a night of wint'ry fog.
&nbsp;

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:30.800
In a shot surely inspired by the Lord of the&nbsp;
Rings, four shrouded riders flee the scene. 
&nbsp;

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:35.680
..and If you played the network test, you&nbsp;
might have even faced one of them. At night,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:40.080
on a bridge, this exact same shrouded&nbsp;
horse and rider, can be found. 
&nbsp;

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:47.520
The Rune of Death was stolen.
But here's where things get interesting:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:54.640
So runes are letters of a runic alphabet..and in&nbsp;
fantasy, they're often markings of great power.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.640 --> 00:01:01.440
The Elden Ring is actually made up of runes - its&nbsp;
tiniest pieces are a currency like Souls..but its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:08.960
larger shards are called "Great Runes" , and&nbsp;
they are far more significant. Together, these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:15.760
Great Runes of the Elden Ring spell out a Golden&nbsp;
Order for the world. Japanese descriptions call&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:23.760
it a Golden Law. A logic, for life to follow. 
Now, this Golden Order is broken to its core..and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:27.120
it all began, when the Rune&nbsp;
of Death of stolen. 
&nbsp;

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:31.680
So what was the Rune of Death,&nbsp;
and why was its theft important&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:36.400
enough to spark The Shattering? 
Well..I think items in the Network Test&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:41.840
hold the clue. In Elden Ring, there's an item&nbsp;
called a Holy Pot, something you can throw at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:48.880
undead enemies to prevent them from rising after&nbsp;
death. It reads "Incantations of the Golden Order&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:56.400
have been stored inside", "The Golden Order&nbsp;
has no mercy for those who trespass beyond&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.400 --> 00:02:01.600
life's bounds", and its Japanese description&nbsp;
clarifies that "The Golden Law does not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:07.920
permit the logic to live in death". 
With the Rune of Death stolen from the Elden Ring,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:14.320
nothing is keeping the dead in their graves.&nbsp;
That law doesn't bind undeath..not any more. Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:21.280
spirits are found all throughout the Lands&nbsp;
between. Now, skeletons stand from their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:26.320
graves. Even you, the Tarnished are&nbsp;
called "ye dead who yet live". 
&nbsp;

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:36.240
This lawless world has given rise to a group&nbsp;
called the "Golden Order Fundamentalists" who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:42.560
try to enforce the old laws of the Elden Ring.&nbsp;
One of their spells is "Litany of Proper Death",&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:49.600
an incantation that prevents undead&nbsp;
enemies from coming back to life.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:55.120
So this Golden Law can still be applied..it's&nbsp;
just not a universal truth any more. 
&nbsp;

00:02:55.120 --> 00:03:02.160
Before the Shattering, the Lands Between&nbsp;
were ruled by Queen Marika "the Eternal".&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:08.960
Her being "Eternal", suggests that the Elden Ring&nbsp;
wasn't applying death to the Queen or her Demigod&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:15.120
children. However, now that seems set to change&nbsp;
- because the Rune of Death has been stolen, 
&nbsp;

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:17.840
And the demigods began to fall. 
&nbsp;

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:25.280
Surely it's no coincidence that only now, death&nbsp;
is being served to Marika's demi-god children.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:28.880
A thief holds the Rune of&nbsp;
Death..and it's being used -
&nbsp;

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:34.000
Starting with Godwyn the Golden.
In Dark Souls, all of Gwyn's children,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:39.440
start with the same name prefix..you&nbsp;
know, Gwyndolin, Gwynevere..just so,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:44.960
all of Queen Marika's children appear to have&nbsp;
names that start with the "God" prefix. So far&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:50.720
we know of two others: Goddrick, the demi-god&nbsp;
boss at the end of Stormveil Castle..Godfrey,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:56.720
who we haven't seen yet, but who ruled over&nbsp;
his own age..and now..Godwyn the Golden.
&nbsp;

00:03:56.720 --> 00:04:02.160
A shadow looms over Godwyn - and it kind of looks&nbsp;
like a person holding a large weapon. When they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:08.000
retreat, they take the light with them, and in the&nbsp;
darkness, emerging from the strangely shaped wound&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:15.200
on their back, a writhing force worms its way&nbsp;
around their body, and towards their eyes. 
&nbsp;

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:20.400
With this, Godwyn seems to live again after&nbsp;
death. As we mentioned earlier, undeath is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:25.360
possible now..though we have no idea who he&nbsp;
serves. And while all this is going on...
&nbsp;

00:04:26.320 --> 00:04:31.120
Queen Marika was driven to the brink.
But she doesn't seem to have been killed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:38.160
Yet. We, as "Tarnished" are even able to&nbsp;
resurrect at her statues..suggesting that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:44.800
she's still a force in the world, and that she&nbsp;
has an affection, or at least a use, for us. 
&nbsp;

00:04:46.560 --> 00:04:50.080
In the scene to follow, her crown&nbsp;
is set upon an empty throne.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:55.840
I say its hers, because this main&nbsp;
throne is surrounded by five..maybe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.840 --> 00:05:01.200
6 other, smaller thrones - likely&nbsp;
those of her demi-god children. 
&nbsp;

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:07.520
The throne itself is embossed with countless&nbsp;
depictions of the Erdtree. And we need&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.520 --> 00:05:13.840
to talk about the Erdtree..because it's a symbol&nbsp;
of Queen Marika's power way more than the Elden&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.840 --> 00:05:19.840
Ring is. The age before the Shattering&nbsp;
is called "The Age of the Erdtree", after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:24.240
all [Source: Telescope description]. It's not&nbsp;
called the age of the Elden Ring. The Elden Ring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.240 --> 00:05:30.320
is just the source of the Erdtree's power - and&nbsp;
it's the Erdtree and Marika's family that seems&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.320 --> 00:05:38.400
to direct that power, delivering Golden Grace&nbsp;
to certain folk of the Lands Between. But again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:43.360
we talk about that more in another video.
This scene is clearly meant to symbolise an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:48.720
absence of that power now that the shattering&nbsp;
war has begun. And the last to leave this throne&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.720 --> 00:05:55.120
room..is Margitt the Fell Omen. This is clearly&nbsp;
him - The main boss of Elden Ring's network test,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.760 --> 00:06:02.320
guardian of Stormveil castle..and now&nbsp;
perhaps..a servant of Marika's Royal Family?
&nbsp;

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:06.880
The Elden Ring Twitter revealed that&nbsp;
"The cursemarks he bore from birth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:12.880
were another ominous sign for the royal family".&nbsp;
This proves he was close to them, and explains his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.880 --> 00:06:20.720
name - Margitt was a fell omen for Marika's royal&nbsp;
family..a sign of the terrible things to come. 
&nbsp;

00:06:20.720 --> 00:06:24.560
The Shattering ensued; a war&nbsp;
that wrought only darkness.
&nbsp;

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:31.760
The Elden Ring was broken,&nbsp;
but by whom? And why?
&nbsp;

00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:39.200
So whoever broke the Elden Ring..hasn't publicly&nbsp;
revealed themselves, or made a play for its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:44.240
power, even now. It follows then, that their&nbsp;
goal might have just been to watch chaos unfold.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.240 --> 00:06:49.360
The Great Rune of Death is just one part&nbsp;
of the puzzle - imagine how many other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.360 --> 00:06:55.760
Laws have been thrown into disarray.&nbsp;
Now, estranged demi-gods holding other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.760 --> 00:07:00.320
Great Runes [source: official website] are&nbsp;
warring amongst eachother. Why interfere? 
&nbsp;

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:04.880
What could the demigods ever&nbsp;
hope to win by warring?
&nbsp;

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:11.680
This scene is so incredible..the absolute scale&nbsp;
of it. Under the shadow of a very sad-looking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:21.840
Erdtree, besieging a fortress with statues&nbsp;
of Tree Sentinels..is a force familiar to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.840 --> 00:07:28.160
any who played the Network Test. These soldiers&nbsp;
and giants are seen all throughout Limgrave,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.160 --> 00:07:33.120
and their lion heraldry likely&nbsp;
marks them as warriors of Godrick,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:39.760
one of Marika's demi-god children, and the ruler&nbsp;
of Stormveil castle. He's clearly waging war&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:45.360
against a city of the Erdtree - something&nbsp;
that would have been his former home. 
&nbsp;

00:07:45.920 --> 00:07:50.400
According to the Elden Ring Twitter,&nbsp;
Godrick was "born a weakling child,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:56.400
and coveted the strength of his kin". His "kingdom&nbsp;
is still at war long past the shattering"..and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.400 --> 00:08:03.360
he "clings to his ruined legacy, the ruler of a&nbsp;
husk wrung dry by war". Clearly he wields a lot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.360 --> 00:08:09.280
of power..but that power is waning - "Godrick's&nbsp;
claim as the rightful golden king is not wholly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.280 --> 00:08:14.640
uncontested. There are those who plot to see&nbsp;
his crown pass into more worthy hands". 
&nbsp;

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:25.840
Even after the shattering, powerful&nbsp;
individuals remain. Like these two. 
&nbsp;

00:08:34.160 --> 00:08:48.880
The conqueror of the stars, General Radahn,
And the Blade of Miquella, Malenia the Severed
&nbsp;

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:54.880
First thing here..very important..General Radahn&nbsp;
has a goddamn horse between his legs. Yup.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.680 --> 00:08:57.101
That is one sad fucking horse. I know&nbsp;
From Software tell some tragic stories,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.101 --> 00:09:00.080
but man..this is on another level. 
Lucky for the horse, Radahn appears&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.080 --> 00:09:01.200
to have gravitational powers..so&nbsp;
hopefully he's using these powers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:04.480
on himself. Let me explain how I know&nbsp;
that: when you cast spells in Elden Ring,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.480 --> 00:09:10.640
the class of spell is revealed by the symbol&nbsp;
that pops up..and the symbol for gravitational&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.640 --> 00:09:17.760
sorcery is revealed - here. And look..It's the&nbsp;
exact same symbol embossed onto his blades.
&nbsp;

00:09:17.760 --> 00:09:23.040
The purple glow between his blades is even the&nbsp;
same that purple gravitational sorcery gets.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.040 --> 00:09:29.120
For example, this is the meteorite spell. The&nbsp;
meteorite item description reads "meteorites held&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.120 --> 00:09:35.520
the same import as stars"..and Radahn is clearly&nbsp;
capable of channeling that cosmic power. 
&nbsp;

00:09:35.520 --> 00:09:41.280
Remember the first trailer, we ever saw? 
Ohh elden ring. That which commanded the stars.
&nbsp;

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:46.720
The Elden Ring commanded the stars..and&nbsp;
Radahn conquered them. I guess that would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.720 --> 00:09:54.400
make him a warrior of the Elden&nbsp;
Ring, right? In another video,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:54.400 --> 00:10:00.480
we'll talk about the age of cosmic power that&nbsp;
came before the Age of the Erdtree..but for now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:00.480 --> 00:10:04.560
just know that this age did exist&nbsp;
long ago, before the Elden Ring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.560 --> 00:10:07.520
commanded the stars. This completes our rough&nbsp;
timeline. Anyway, back to the shattering.
&nbsp;

00:10:07.520 --> 00:10:11.680
These two were the mightiest to&nbsp;
remain, and locked horns in combat. 
&nbsp;

00:10:15.280 --> 00:10:20.160
He hacks off Miquela's prosthetic arm..but she&nbsp;
snatches the blade attached to that arm out of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.160 --> 00:10:25.520
thin air, and uses her own body weight&nbsp;
to force it deeper into Radahn's flesh.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:31.360
While doing this..she's muttering something -&nbsp;
an incantation maybe? I do think it's Miquela&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:31.360 --> 00:10:39.200
who summons this orange lotus - it snakes in from&nbsp;
behind her, and probably teleports her away. 
&nbsp;

00:10:40.480 --> 00:10:49.360
But there would be no victor.
We get to fight Miquela later on,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.360 --> 00:10:54.160
so obviously she survives this encounter&nbsp;
- though I'm not so sure about Radahn.
&nbsp;

00:10:54.960 --> 00:10:58.960
While the dialogue implies that neither one&nbsp;
of them lost this fight..remember - in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:58.960 --> 00:11:03.360
first trailer, we see Radahn get struck&nbsp;
by this lance knight on horseback..so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:03.920 --> 00:11:13.840
perhaps there's more to this cutscene that we&nbsp;
haven't yet seen. For now, here's the finale.
&nbsp;

00:11:14.640 --> 00:11:20.880
And so, we inhabit a fractured world.
This character, is the storyteller. Wait that's my&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:20.880 --> 00:11:30.720
job - anyway..on her right is a projection of her&nbsp;
self - a mirror image that shares her right eye.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:30.720 --> 00:11:37.360
What's fascinating about this..is that Melina, our&nbsp;
maiden..also has a closed eye with a marking. 
&nbsp;

00:11:38.000 --> 00:11:43.360
Some people have pointed out that this marking&nbsp;
is on Melina's left eye..whereas this storyteller&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:43.360 --> 00:11:51.280
has the marking on her right - but remember - the&nbsp;
Melina we see is an apparition. She appears out of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:51.280 --> 00:11:57.280
a blue, ghostly form..meaning she's actually&nbsp;
closer to this phantom storyteller..rather&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:57.280 --> 00:12:03.200
than the real one. Therefore, the marking&nbsp;
might actually be on the right side&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:04.240 --> 00:12:10.320
for both of them..if that makes sense.
Anyway..the world has been fractured. Even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:13.360 --> 00:12:17.120
characters..like Melina and the&nbsp;
Storyteller..are stuck in a sort of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:17.120 --> 00:12:31.200
limbo between life and death. Fractured.
Awaiting the arrival of the Elden Lord.
&nbsp;

00:12:31.200 --> 00:12:32.160
Unless of course,
&nbsp;

